{"id": "tea:aptamimamsa:1", "source": "src:aptamimamsa", "location": {"ref": "1", "section": null}, "original": {"text": "devāgamanabhoyānacāmarādivibhūtayaḥ / māyāviṣv api dṛśyante nātas tvam asi no mahān", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled by the unit author (wording believed standard; to be checked against an edition)", "licence": "public-domain text"}, "paraphrase": "The coming of the gods, travel through the sky, the fly-whisks and other splendours are seen even in magicians; not for these are you great to us.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "powers-experiences"], "concepts": ["cpt:labdhis-rddhis", "cpt:sadguru-marks"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Outward wonders do not qualify a teacher; only faultlessness and omniscience do.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:aptamimamsa:104", "source": "src:aptamimamsa", "location": {"ref": "104", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Syādvāda, which gives up absolute one-sidedness, is the method of affirming 'in some respect' (kathaṃcit).", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:syadvada", "trm:syat", "trm:ekanta"], "concepts": ["cpt:syadvada-saptabhangi"], "obstacles": ["obs:ekanta-view"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:aptamimamsa:105", "source": "src:aptamimamsa", "location": {"ref": "105", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Syādvāda and omniscience both illumine all realities; they differ only as indirect and direct; what neither illumines is not a real thing.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language", "consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:syadvada", "trm:kevala-jnana"], "concepts": ["cpt:syadvada-saptabhangi", "cpt:kevala-jnana"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:aptamimamsa:14", "source": "src:aptamimamsa", "location": {"ref": "14", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "[For you] a thing is in some respect existent, in some respect non-existent, [in some respect] both, and inexpressible — by joining the standpoints, not absolutely.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["ultimate", "sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:syadvada", "trm:saptabhangi", "trm:syat", "trm:avaktavya"], "concepts": ["cpt:syadvada-saptabhangi", "cpt:anekantavada"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:aptamimamsa:24-27", "source": "src:aptamimamsa", "location": {"ref": "24-27", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Absolute non-duality is refuted: if all were one, there would be no distinction of act and fruit, merit and demerit, this world and the next, knowledge and ignorance, bondage and liberation; and non-duality cannot be proved without admitting a second.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:jain-views-of-other-darsanas", "cpt:anekantavada"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "disputes": ["dsp:souls-one-or-distinct", "dsp:world-real-or-appearance"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse range recalled (second pariccheda).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:aptamimamsa:4", "source": "src:aptamimamsa", "location": {"ref": "4", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The faults and the coverings [of knowledge] can be entirely destroyed in someone, because they are seen to diminish by degrees — as the outer and inner impurity [of gold] is removed by its proper causes.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["dispute", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:kevala-jnana"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "disputes": ["dsp:omniscience"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:aptamimamsa:5", "source": "src:aptamimamsa", "location": {"ref": "5", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Things subtle, remote in time and distant in space are directly perceived by someone, because they are inferable, like fire; thus the omniscient one is established.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["dispute", "consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:sarvajna"], "concepts": ["cpt:kevala-jnana"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "disputes": ["dsp:omniscience"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:aptamimamsa:6", "source": "src:aptamimamsa", "location": {"ref": "6", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "You alone are that faultless one, whose speech does not conflict with reason and scripture.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:sadguru-marks"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:aptamimamsa:pariccheda-3", "source": "src:aptamimamsa", "location": {"ref": "pariccheda-3", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The one-sided views of permanence and of momentariness are both refuted: a merely permanent thing could not act or change, and a merely momentary one could not bear karma, memory, or its fruit.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute", "world-fate"], "concepts": ["cpt:utpada-vyaya-dhrauvya", "cpt:anekantavada"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "disputes": ["dsp:momentariness", "dsp:is-there-a-self"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
